# The whole graphify knowledge graph is machine-regenerable (AST-only, no
# API cost -- `graphify update .`, also run automatically by its post-commit
# hook) and churns on nearly every commit, so tracking it just produces
# large diffs unrelated to the actual change and merge conflicts between
# concurrent branches/sessions. Not worth committing.
graphify-out/

prompts

